 3
Write a PL/SQL program that prompts for EMPNO and deletes
the employee from EMP table.
Handle using User Defined Exception.
====================================================================

SQL Command:
------------

sql> ACCEPT P_EMPNO PROMPT 'Enter Employee Number : '

sql> DECLARE

EMP_NOT_FOUND EXCEPTION;

BEGIN

DELETE FROM EMP
WHERE EMPNO=&P_EMPNO;

IF SQL%ROWCOUNT=0 THEN
RAISE EMP_NOT_FOUND;
END IF;

COMMIT;

DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Employee Deleted.');

EXCEPTION

WHEN EMP_NOT_FOUND THEN

DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE
('Employee Number Not Found.');

END;
/

Output (Valid EMPNO):
---------------------

Enter Employee Number : 7900

Employee Deleted.

PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


Output (Invalid EMPNO):
-----------------------

Enter Employee Number : 9999

Employee Number Not Found.

PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


